# Fixed 2026-09-30, defect 131's class, lane recovery-b2 (lane recovery-b1's
# report, U4), beside `fixedbugs-131-a-bracket-the-lexer-found-open-in-a-literal`.
# Symptom: a group, a call's arguments, an index, or a literal inside another,
# whose opener the lexer found never closed, named the missing closer beside
# the lexer's `unclosed_bracket`, one mistake and two messages: `x = (1 + 2`
# over `print(x)` cost `expected_group_close` at `print`, `xs = [[1], [2`
# cost `expected_separator` at the end of the block, and `foo(1, (2 + 3` four
# messages for its two openers. Cause: only a literal and a type asked the
# lexer's question (`parse/unclosed.hero`), and a literal inside another took
# the line end it ended at, so the one around it found none. Now each ends at
# the line end no `,` goes on from, leaves it where it stands, and names no
# closer: the lexer's report is the one message, and a mistake after it on
# its own line is still told. One shape per function.

function a_group()
    x = (1 + 2  #~ unclosed_bracket
    print(x)

function a_call()
    print(1, 2  #~ unclosed_bracket
    print(3)

